-- title:
--   Relative ramification and inertia degrees in a tower of local fields
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $K_w \subseteq L_w$ be two intermediate fields of the extension $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q$ (with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ the algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl q` carrying its canonical valuation), each finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, the hypothesis $K_w \le L_w$ being given. For a finite level $F$, write $R_F =$ `Rw q F` for the valuation subring of $F$ obtained by pulling back, along the structure map $F \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$, the valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ attached to its canonical $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$-valued valuation; thus $R_F$ is the closed unit ball of $F$. The assertion is that there exist natural numbers $e, f$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota : R_{K_w} \to R_{L_w}$ such that: $\iota$ is compatible with the embeddings into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$, i.e. the image of $x \in R_{K_w}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ via $\iota$ and $L_w$ equals the image of $x$ via $K_w$; $e > 0$ and $f > 0$; the ideal of $R_{L_w}$ generated by the image under $\iota$ of the maximal ideal of the local ring $R_{K_w}$ is the $e$-th power of the maximal ideal of $R_{L_w}$; the cardinality of the residue field of $R_{L_w}$ is the $f$-th power of that of the residue field of $R_{K_w}$; and $[L_w : \mathbb{Q}_q] = [K_w : \mathbb{Q}_q] \cdot (e f)$.
--
--   This is the fundamental identity $e(L_w/K_w) f(L_w/K_w) = [L_w : K_w]$ for the unique prime of $R_{L_w}$ above the maximal ideal of $R_{K_w}$, stated in tower-law form so that no $K_w$-algebra structure on $L_w$ needs to be fixed, the comparison map $\iota$ being pinned down by its compatibility with the embeddings into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$. It serves the local analysis of levels, feeding the statements about residue-field cardinalities and Frobenius powers used there, such as [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.aeval_pow_card_residueField_minpoly_eq_zero`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.aeval_pow_card_residueField_minpoly_eq_zero), [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.exists_eq_pow_card_pow_of_mem_rootSet`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.exists_eq_pow_card_pow_of_mem_rootSet) and [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.eq_of_unramified_level_of_index_eq`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.eq_of_unramified_level_of_index_eq).
